Key remapping in mapped types using an `as` clause was introduced in **TypeScript 4.1** (released November 2020), along with template literal types. For example:

```ts
type Getters<T> = {
  [K in keyof T as `get${Capitalize<string & K>}`]: () => T[K]
};
```

You can also filter keys by remapping them to `never`.

