Use `string`, not `String`.

The docs say never to use the types `Number`, `String`, `Boolean`, `Symbol`, or `Object`. They refer to non-primitive boxed objects that are almost never used appropriately in JavaScript code. Use `number`, `string`, `boolean`, and `symbol` instead. In place of `Object`, use the non-primitive `object` type.

```ts
/* WRONG */
function reverse(s: String): String;

/* OK */
function reverse(s: string): string;
```

